  "context_pill": "Section 35AD & Section 73A",
  "example_summary": "XYZ Ltd operates a Madurai Hotel and Coimbatore Hotel, computing 35AD deduction and Section 73A set-off.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 35AD & Section 73A\n\n| Provision / Section | Eligible Activity / Scope | Qualifying Expenditure & Exclusions | Set-off & Carry Forward Rule |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 35AD** | Specified businesses including new hotels (two-star or above) | 100% deduction for capital expenditure (excluding land, goodwill, financial instruments) | Loss can be set-off **only** against another specified business under Section 73A |\n| **Section 73A** | Specified businesses under Section 35AD | Pre-commencement capital expenditure capitalized as on date of commencement qualifies | Unabsorbed specified business loss can be carried forward indefinitely for set-off against specified business income |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Land Exclusion Rule: Expenditure incurred on the acquisition of land or goodwill or financial instruments does not qualify for deduction under Section 35AD.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Set-off Restriction: Loss from a specified business under Section 35AD can never be set off against normal business profits or any other head of income; it is exclusively restricted to profits from another specified business under Section 73A.",
